  "final_message": "I built the XML checker app and ran the API checks against it, but I couldn't build or run the Docker image because Docker isn't available in this sandbox. Outside Docker, the API checks in `tests/smoke_test.py` all pass. The frontend typechecks and builds, and gunicorn served the health check, the frontend and an XML check correctly. I didn't try the web pages in a browser.\n\n**Backend:**\n- **The checker** (`backend/xmlcheck.py`) uses Python's built-in XML parser and only reads the submitted text. It never loads external files, DTDs or entities, and it stops documents that try to blow up through nested entity expansion. The `column` it reports starts at 1.\n- **The API** (`backend/app.py`) covers all the endpoints in the spec, with SQLite stored in `./data/app.db`.\n- **Sign-in:** login returns a random token, and only a hash of it is stored. Missing or invalid tokens get 401. Passwords are stored hashed.\n- **Error codes:** registering a username that's taken gets 409. Trying to delete another user's check gets 404, the same as a check that doesn't exist.\n- **Saved-check list:** the `valid` filter takes `true` or `false`, and `page_size` defaults to 20 with a maximum of 100.\n- **Additions not in the spec:** `GET /api/auth/me`, `POST /api/auth/logout` and `GET /api/validations/{id}`. Any API error returns JSON of the form `{\"error\": ...}`.\n\n**Frontend** (React and TypeScript, styled only with Tailwind classes):\n- Sign-in and registration tabs, plus the signed-in username and a sign-out button in the header.\n- A text area with line numbers, file loading, Clear, and a Check button (Ctrl/Cmd+Enter also works).\n- A valid result shows the green \"Well-formed\" badge with the root element. An error shows the message and its position, highlights that line and column, and clicking the position moves the cursor there.\n- Signed-in users get a Save switch, which starts off, and a saved-checks panel with All/Valid/Invalid filters, delete buttons and paging.\n\n**Dependencies:** I added Tailwind, `@tailwindcss/vite`, TypeScript and the React type packages at fixed versions and updated `package-lock.json`. The Python dependencies didn't change.\n\nI also added a `.gitignore`, a `typecheck` npm script and a short Development section in `README.md`.",
  "final_message_truncated": false,
